# Console OIDC login (Authorization Code + PKCE). Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
# Leave these unset to disable OIDC and use manual token-paste (local development).
#
# The id_token the console obtains is sent to the kernel as the bearer; the kernel's OIDC
# IdentityPort (adapters/identity/oidc.py) verifies it (issuer + audience + rotating JWKS).
# IMPORTANT: the kernel's configured `audience` must equal VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID below.

# Required to enable OIDC:
VITE_OIDC_ISSUER=https://dev-12345.okta.com/oauth2/default
VITE_OIDC_CLIENT_ID=0oaEXAMPLEclientid

# Optional (sensible defaults shown):
# VITE_OIDC_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/callback
# VITE_OIDC_SCOPES=openid profile email
# VITE_OIDC_TENANT_CLAIM=tenant

# Optional — skip OIDC discovery by pinning endpoints explicitly:
# VITE_OIDC_AUTH_ENDPOINT=https://.../authorize
# VITE_OIDC_TOKEN_ENDPOINT=https://.../token

# Dev API proxy target (used by vite.config.ts; defaults to http://localhost:8000):
# KERNEL_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
